---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Code of Conduct" description="How we expect people to treat each other in the Brik & Bytes community.">
  <div class="page-header">
    <h1>Code of Conduct</h1>
    <p class="empty-note">Applies everywhere the community gathers — Discord, events, and anywhere else we show up together.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-prose">
    <h2>Be respectful</h2>
    <p>
      Disagree with ideas, not people. Harassment, discrimination, and personal attacks of any
      kind — based on background, identity, experience level, or anything else — aren't
      tolerated.
    </p>

    <h2>Be helpful</h2>
    <p>
      Everyone was a beginner once. Questions that seem obvious to you might not be to someone
      else — answer kindly, or point to where they can find out.
    </p>

    <h2>No spam or self-promotion without context</h2>
    <p>
      Sharing your own work, job openings, or projects is welcome — just keep it relevant and
      don't flood channels with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting an issue</h2>
    <p>
      If something happens that breaks this code — in the Discord, at an event, or anywhere
      else — reach out to a moderator directly on Discord. Reports are handled privately.
    </p>

    <p class="empty-note">
      This is a living document, adapted from common open-source community codes of conduct —
      suggest changes via a PR on <a href="https://github.com/briknbytes">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
